  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Epidemiekontrolle und Gesundheitssystemst&#xe4;rkung</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">epidemic control and health system strengthening</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Epidemiekontrolle und St&#xe4;rkung des Gesundheitssystems</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Phase III, the core areas (1) and (2) are to be continued and the approach consolidated. In core area (1), in addition to consolidating the early warning system for epidemics, there will be a focus on expanding small-scale WASH infrastructure for additional health facilities in order to reduce the risk of epidemics spreading through adequate hygiene facilities. In the core area (2), there will be increased collaboration of community-based organisations on family planning, including early pregnancy prevention, sexual violence prevention and HIV/AIDS prevention. Due to the enormous need in this area, further engagement in social marketing with the national AIDS secretariat seems to make sense. This will result in improved integration and consolidate prevention measures against HIV/AIDS and promotional activities for the target group. In addition, it is planned to fund buildings for emergency obstetric care to the district hospital in Kambia in close cooperation with TC. Furthermore, the ownership of the Sierra Leonean partners is to be increased so that they can continue the project as independently as possible in the medium and long term.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">In Phase III sollen weiterhin die Kernbereiche (1) und (2) fortgef&#xfc;hrt und der Ansatz konsolidiert werden. Im Kernbereich (1) soll neben der Konsolidierung des Fr&#xfc;hwarnsystems f&#xfc;r Epidemien ein Schwerpunkt auf dem Ausbau von kleiner WASH Infrastruktur f&#xfc;r weitere Gesundheitseinrichtungen liegen, um das Risiko der Aus- und Verbreitung von Epidemien durch angemessene Hygienevorrichtungen zu reduzieren. Im Kernbereich (2) soll eine verst&#xe4;rkte Zusammenarbeit von gemeindebasierten Organisationen zum Thema Familienplanung erfolgen und auch die Bereiche Verh&#xfc;tung von Fr&#xfc;hschwangerschaften, Vermeidung sexueller Gewalt und Pr&#xe4;vention von HIV/AIDS einbeziehen. Aufgrund des enormen Bedarfs in diesem Bereich erscheint ein weiteres Engagement im Bereich Social Marketing mit dem nationalen AIDS-Sekretariat sinnvoll. Damit werden Pr&#xe4;ventionsma&#xdf;nahmen gegen HIV/AIDS und Promotionsaktivit&#xe4;ten f&#xfc;r Betroffene besser integriert und konsolidiert. Zus&#xe4;tzlich ist angedacht, in enger Zusammenarbeit mit der TZ, das Distriktkrankenhaus in Kambia um Geb&#xe4;ude f&#xfc;r die geburtshilfliche Notfallversorgung zu erg&#xe4;nzen. Dar&#xfc;ber hinaus soll das Ownership der sierra-leonischen Partner erh&#xf6;ht werden, damit diese mittel- und langfristig das Vorhaben m&#xf6;glichst eigenst&#xe4;ndig fortf&#xfc;hren k&#xf6;nnen</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Phase III, the core areas (1) and (2) are to be continued and the approach consolidated. In core area (1), in addition to consolidating the early warning system for epidemics, there will be a focus on expanding small-scale WASH infrastructure for additional health facilities in order to reduce the risk of epidemics spreading through adequate hygiene facilities. In the core area (2), there will be increased collaboration of community-based organisations on family planning, including early pregnancy prevention, sexual violence prevention and HIV/AIDS prevention. Due to the enormous need in this area, further engagement in social marketing with the national AIDS secretariat seems to make sense. This will result in improved integration and consolidate prevention measures against HIV/AIDS and promotional activities for the target group. In addition, it is planned to fund buildings for emergency obstetric care to the district hospital in Kambia in close cooperation with TC. Furthermore, the ownership of the Sierra Leonean partners is to be increased so that they can continue the project as independently as possible in the medium and long term.</narrative>
  </description>
